  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EPIPHANY CARE FOUNDATION LIVELIHOODIMPROVEMENT GRANT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The prevention of hunger and the improvement of livelihoods &#x2013; in the areas of food security and resilience aims to address the challenges faced by communities in Numan and Magadali LGAs of Adamawa state, Nigeria, particularly during periods of flooding. This initiative focuses on two key objectives: Firstly, to ensure that vulnerable populations have access to sufficient and nutritious food to prevent hunger and malnutrition during flooding events. Secondly, to enhance the resilience of these communities by promoting sustainable livelihood opportunities that can withstand the impact of floods and contribute to long-term food security.</narrative>
  </description>
